<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Plan 4 Task 7: adaptive icon MONOCHROME layer (API 33+ "themed icons" / Material You - system
  Settings > Wallpaper & style > Themed icons). Same 3 shapes/coordinates as
  ic_launcher_foreground.xml (ring + shield + dot - see that file's own kdoc for the full geometry
  rationale), but every fillColor/strokeColor here is opaque white: per Android's own themed-icon
  guidance, the system reads ONLY this layer's alpha channel and re-tints the visible pixels with
  its own dynamic accent color, so the literal color is inert (same "alpha channel is all that
  matters" rule ic_notification.xml/ic_stat_terrawatch.xml document for notification small icons) -
  white is used here purely by convention (fully opaque wherever a shape is drawn, fully transparent
  elsewhere).
-->
